WEBVTT

NOTE Cedwyn film, scene 001 "Place-names before the deeds", en. Timings from the rendered audio.

1
00:00:03.500 --> 00:00:13.048
<v Nia>Bore da. Gloves on before you touch anything. Before a single deed, we've got names. Just names, written in your family's research notes.

2
00:00:14.044 --> 00:00:27.413
<v The Grandson>Cedwyn. That's the word I keep tripping over. Cedwyn, Cwm-Cedwyn, Nant-Cedwyn, Ynys-Cedwyn. Then Cedfin, Cydfin, Cydwin. And Tŷ Mawr, the Great House.

3
00:00:27.713 --> 00:00:41.933
<v Nia>This is the index. Six research leads, GHF-E174 to GHF-E179. It shows where each name turns up, and which notes lean on which. Pull one out, you see what wobbles.

4
00:00:42.362 --> 00:00:48.989
<v The Grandson>So does it prove the Great House stood on Cedwyn land? That my family's roots there go back before any deed?

5
00:00:50.369 --> 00:01:03.146
<v Nia>Not on its own. It proves the leads are catalogued. Whether the variants are one place, whether they mean Tŷ Mawr, and what any old lease meant for the land after 1877: those are the next checks.

6
00:01:05.711 --> 00:01:12.828
<v The Grandson>Cwm-Cedwyn. A wooded dell on the Ely, between Leckwith and Llandough. My notes use it all the time.

7
00:01:13.961 --> 00:01:24.658
<v Nia>They do. But there's no source attached yet. We don't know when the name was first written, where its edges ran, or whether it ever touched Tŷ Mawr. Checking is still to do.

8
00:01:31.159 --> 00:01:35.599
<v The Grandson>And Nant-Cedwyn. A brook running into the Ely near Leckwith.

9
00:01:35.899 --> 00:01:49.236
<v Nia>That one points to a primary document, and we haven't got it yet. So for now it shows us one thing: the family noted the name. Name, place, date, link to Tŷ Mawr: all still to be checked.

10
00:01:50.439 --> 00:01:52.442
<v The Grandson>Ynys-Cedwyn's the odd one out.

11
00:01:52.975 --> 00:02:01.571
<v Nia>Ynys-Cedwyn sits up where the Twrch meets the Tawe, a long way from here. The note ties it to Cedwyn Gawr, Cedwyn the Giant.

12
00:02:01.871 --> 00:02:06.631
<v The Grandson>A giant. Lovely. Is there anything linking him to Llandough?

13
00:02:06.931 --> 00:02:14.814
<v Nia>Not yet. No primary source, the place and the giant both waiting to be checked, and no link to Tŷ Mawr written down.

14
00:02:15.457 --> 00:02:18.735
<v The Grandson>So the film starts with a name we can't pin down.

15
00:02:19.392 --> 00:02:25.665
<v Nia>It starts honest. A name, and a hill that came before it. Let's go and stand on the hill.
